.specify/bridge-events.jsonl
# Per-working-copy Spec Kit state, not project source: which feature THIS checkout is on,
# and the live bridge handoff (status + artifact hashes, rewritten constantly by tooling).
# Tracking them made every feature branch collide on the same two files. Both are recreated
# on demand by the speckit scripts, so removing them from version control costs nothing.
.specify/feature.json
.specify/superpowers-handoff.json
*.stackdump
test-results/
playwright-report/
# Playwright sharding (issue #75): per-shard blob output and the merge job's staging dir.
# Sharding is gone (034 FR-057); these stay only so an older checkout's leftovers are still ignored.
blob-report/
all-blob-reports/
.last-run.json
# The JSON run report. `docs/testing.md` tells developers to write this to the repo root to get
# per-file durations (034 SC-015), and `release.yml` writes it on CI — so the documented procedure
# produces it by design, and without this line it would sit untracked waiting to be committed by
# accident. It is a measurement of a run, not source.
e2e-report.json

# Installer verification verdict (020): a generated CI artifact, not source.
verification-verdict.json
# 042: one verdict per artifact role, and whatever `--verdict-out` was pointed at. A verification
# run writes wherever it is told, and the obvious short name lands in the repo root — which is one
# `git add -A` from being committed, as it duly was.
verification-verdict-*.json
/v.json
# Scratch from scripts/run-deelevated.ps1 if a run is interrupted
deelevated-*.log
deelevated-*.cmd
deelevated-*.code

# 030 FR-058 — the notice-subject guard compiles throwaway fixtures with tsc, under
# `packages/ui/tests/` so module resolution matches the real renderer's. It removes them in
# `afterAll`, so the directory only survives a run that was interrupted — and then a later
# `git add -A` picks up generated files as though they were source.
packages/ui/tests/.tsc-notice-guard/
